chen: quick one — my docs PR (#487) is blocked on a runtime clarification. The SDK snippet for streaming + function calling assumes the server will fallback to a non-streaming full response on transient model errors, but zach said the runtime might just terminate the stream with an error. which behavior should we document?

oliver: @chen can you paste the snippet? i want to make sure the example matches what we ship.

chen: sure — here's the snippet i'm using in the doc: 
```js
const resp = await client.chat.stream({
  model: 'redwood-codegen-1',
  messages,
  functions: [myFunctionSpec],
  stream: true,
});
for await (const chunk of resp) {
  if (chunk.function_call) {
    // call the tool locally
  }
}
```

chen: the question is: if the runtime hits a transient failure after sending some chunks (e.g., OOM on a GPU), does it: 1) close the stream and return an error event only, or 2) transparently switch to a sync/non-streamed response and send the full function_call payload? docs need a clear statement either way.

maria: from a product POV we should recommend authors code defensively for both. but the docs also need a single canonical statement about default runtime behavior.

zach: runtime answer: current runtime does NOT automatically re-run a request as sync on streaming failure. it will close the stream and emit an error frame. we do have a planned feature to support server-side fallback to non-streaming variants but it's not in prod.

oliver: ok thanks @zach — can you confirm the exact error shape we should document (i.e., is it an HTTP 500 with a JSON error frame, or a stream close with no payload)?

zach: it's a stream close with an error frame that follows our streaming error envelope: `{ type: 'error', code: 'internal', message: 'runtime: GPU OOM', details: { transient: true } }` sent as the final chunk, and the HTTP connection closes with 500. i'll paste the exact shape in a follow-up.

chen: that helps. @oliver, should i update the example to show client-side retry/fallback? we can keep the current snippet but add a short note.

oliver: yes add a short note + a minimal defensive pattern. e.g.: 
```js
try {
  for await (const chunk of resp) { /* handle chunk */ }
} catch (err) {
  if (err.code === 'internal' && err.details?.transient) {
    // suggestion: retry once as non-streaming or call the sync API
  }
  throw err
}
```

docs-bot: CI preview: build failed for branch docs/pr-487 — linkcheck OK but docs preview renderer threw an error on streaming code fence (see logs).

deploy-bot: CI / docs-preview failed — https://ci.redwood/preview/487/logs (exit code 1)

maria: is the renderer failure separate? can we unblock the merge if we push the clarifying note and a comment about planned server-side fallback (eta: Q3)?

zach: renderer failure looks unrelated — i'll take a look but it might be the same code fence quirk the preview had last week. i can also add a terse runtime note in the docs to avoid implying automatic server fallback.

chen: i'll push two commits: 1) add the defensive client pattern as oliver suggested, 2) add a short runtime note: "Current runtime closes the stream with an error frame on transient failures; clients should implement retry/fallback patterns. Server-side automatic fallback is a planned feature."

oliver: that should satisfy reviewers. once zach confirms the exact error envelope, add it as an inline code snippet.

zach: confirmed shape will be in my follow-up by EOD.

chen: thanks all — i'll update the PR. @docs-bot can you re-run preview after i push? :thumbsup:

